2. System Architecture

2.1 Encrypted Data Ingestion

Astrophysical datasets are processed through AES‑GCM‑256 with homomorphic extensions. Post‑quantum key management ensures future‑stable security. All species states and astrophysical fields remain encrypted throughout computation.

2.2 Species Definition Matrix

The system defines 100 species fields, each represented as a density function over a spatial grid. Species interactions are encoded in a 100×100 adjacency matrix.

2.3 Interaction Field Solver

Dynamics are governed by coupled PDE/ODE equations evaluated on GPU kernels. The solver supports diffusion, nonlinear interactions, oscillatory coupling, and self‑dynamics.

2.4 Visualization Gateway

A gRPC interface provides real‑time species density plots, stellar overlays, and interaction graph evolution. All outputs remain encrypted until authorized decryption.

